221: ### Requirement 3: Horizontal GPU Scroll Strips (`.strip`), Row Architecture, and Translation Math
222: 
223: #### 3.1 Shelf Hierarchy
224: ```html
225: <section class="row content-shelf" id="shelf-trending-movies">
226:   <h3 class="shelf-title">Trending Movies</h3>
227:   <div class="strip shelf-rail" data-scroll-rail="true">
228:     <!-- 352x198 cards -->
229:   </div>
230: </section>
231: ```
232: 
233: #### 3.2 CSS Rules for High-Performance GPU Compositing
234: ```css
235: .row {
236:   margin-bottom: 18px;
237:   position: relative;
238: }
239: 
240: .row h3,
241: .row .shelf-title {
242:   font-size: 24px;
243:   font-weight: 500;
244:   margin-bottom: 18px;
245:   color: #e8eaed;
246: }
247: 
248: .strip {
249:   white-space: nowrap;
250:   height: 262px;
251:   will-change: transform;
252:   transition: transform .35s cubic-bezier(.2,.8,.2,1);
253: }
254: ```
255: *Height derivation*: $198\text{px} \times 1.1\text{ scale} = 217.8\text{px} + 14\text{px caption margin} + 24\text{px caption font} + 5\text{px halo} = 260.8\text{px}$. The $262\text{px}$ container height provides exact headroom so the scaled focus card and its $30\text{px}$ drop-shadow never clip.
256: 
257: #### 3.3 Horizontal Translation Math (`translateX`)
258: In `.tmp_ref/theboringtv-lgwebos/app.js` (line 467):
259: $$\Delta X = -\max\left(0,\, e.\text{offsetLeft} - (c > 0 \;?\; 40 : 0)\right)$$
260: - **Card 0 ($c = 0$)**: $e.\text{offsetLeft} = 0 \implies \Delta X = 0\text{px}$. The first card aligns cleanly with the left safe margin ($72\text{px}$).
261: - **Card 1 ($c = 1$)**: $e.\text{offsetLeft} = 378\text{px} \implies \Delta X = -(378 - 40) = -338\text{px}$. Card 1 sits at $72 + 40 = 112\text{px}$ from screen left, while Card 0 peeks out by $40\text{px}$ from $72\text{px}$ to $112\text{px}$.
262: - **Card $k$ ($c = k$)**: $e.\text{offsetLeft} = 378k \implies \Delta X = -(378k - 40)\text{px}$.
263: - This $40\text{px}$ offset creates the authentic Google TV "preceding peek" behavior, indicating prior scroll state.
264: 
